WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.310
"Look upon each other"

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.145
"and say the words."

00:00:04.145 --> 00:00:07.230
I would say the challenge with this

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:14.490
sequence was finding a way to present information that at least a good portion of the audience already had

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.540
in a way that was dramatic and exciting.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.029
"The High Septon wed Rhaegar and Lyanna in a secret ceremony."

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.800
There's always meant to be a montage.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.900
"Is this something you can see?"

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.640
The important thing was getting Sam and Bran together because they had

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.780
varying pieces of the puzzle, but they didn't have all the pieces.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.580
"Cut." "Good." "Good."

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.820
"And so you see that actually these were two people in love and that this whole thing that started off"

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.639
"the series Game of Thrones, Robert's Rebellion was a total lie."

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:47.609
John is not just the son of Rhaegar and Lyanna

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.300
but he's the true born son. He's not a bastard.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.300
And that means he's the rightful heir to the Iron Throne, that changes everything.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:54.800
Man!

00:00:55.539 --> 00:01:00.749
It's great to shoot something that's a revelatory moment and then of course the even bigger revelatory moment.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:06.750
I think they both know it's wrong. I think they both know it's gonna cause problems, but it's that thing when you suddenly feel that

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:11.489
deeply about someone it's like a runaway train. You can't stop it happening.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.259
You don't even get the relief of how beautiful it could be or should be. It's not good,

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:19.797
but it should be, but it's not.

00:01:19.797 --> 00:01:24.520
And she's his aunt, so there's that if that kind of thing would bother you.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.430
*fakes gagging* Might be the reaction.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:31.750
I like looking at her and going "Oh god. I'm sorry. Let's, let's go again."

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:40.630
But the fact he is actually heir to the throne, I can lord that over Emilia every day. Every day. *laughs*

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.020
We tried to

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:51.219
contrast the various season endings so that they don't feel too similar. So last season we had a pretty triumphant ending with, um,

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:57.940
Dany finally sailing west towards Westeros. You're supposed to feel like, you know, like fuck yeah.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.490
And this one's like oh...nn...fuck no. *laughs*

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:10.209
As a season closer it's phenomenal and from a directing point of view, okay? How do we do that?

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:17.380
Every year Dan and David have cooked up something that makes us read the outline and the script and just go "Holy

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.600
shit, how the hell are we gonna do this?"

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:26.050
And what really kind of got me super jazzed, I guess, was when we saw the first conceptual paintings.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.510
They're not specific to shots or whatever,

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.810
they're just like "This is the vibe of this scene" and so they'll do this like beautiful

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:36.100
painting of a, of a dragon you know blowing blue flame, blowing a hole in the wall.

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:39.579
You're like "Now I see it. Holy crow. Like that is

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.336
spectacular!"

00:02:41.336 --> 00:02:43.809
And a lot of it is virtual.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.799
There are only so many pieces you can physically shoot.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.279
Of course, whatever we can shoot we did shoot.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:56.940
We have fire elements that were shot, that blast against the wall, wights on green-screen.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:02.800
We have the Night King on a motion base on the back of zombie Viserion.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:07.390
For the ice dragon we looked back at the models that we created.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:13.869
When Tyrion visited the two sick dragons, their ribs are poking through the skin and their skin has become translucent.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:22.690
We added the wound, which is very important, the spear wound that kills him. We also worked on what does his fire look like?

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.999
Because it's not healthy fire. It's, you know, it's a magical evil fire.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.010
This sequence is a real proof of just

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:40.840
the dedication and commitment of that whole team of people working around the world to make something that's impossible and

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.799
unreal seem so real and so present.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.000
"Run! Run! Run!"

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:57.580
I didn't see that coming. Now, like oh oh oh, this is gonna be fun.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:04.719
Winter is here and it's all hitting the fan from all directions.

00:04:07.549 --> 00:04:12.771
Yeah, we've talked a long time about seeing the wall come down. It's all getting real.

00:04:12.771 --> 00:04:14.289
It's suddenly terrifying.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:22.060
They're breaching the wall. You know, it's happening, and it's an amazing thing isn't it.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.170
Hey everybody! Special Game of Thrones episode, so let's break it down.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.130
They do a good job of explaining

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:38.209
some of the more contentious story points and what they intended. A lot of you have asked me about the conspiracy theories surrounding

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:43.759
the beginning of Robert's Rebellion and whether or not Robert found out about the lie and didn't tell anybody.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:49.640
But they also clarify some of the mythology behind Viserion. So just a couple really big questions answered.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.559
And if you didn't know, there's a brand new game of Thrones book that was just published this week.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:59.929
It's a short story about the sons of Aegon the Conquerer. It even mentions one of Samwell Tarly's

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.170
ancestors called

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:06.439
Samwell the Savage. So that book is what the giveaway is going to be for this week. All you have to do to enter that

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.049
is be a subscriber, leave a comment on this video. Obviously

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:13.340
we're doing videos till season 8 gets here, but starting with the Rhaegar and Lyanna stuff.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:18.440
So there weren't as many big questions about the "what", the "why" was the bigger thing here.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.679
And I love the way that they say most of the audience understood.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.290
But they still had to explain it in a visual way.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:29.299
They said they had that problem all the way back in season 1, so this has always been a thing for Game of Thrones, is

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:36.050
that they have to find a way for the show to convey information even if it's common knowledge. So R plus L equals J

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:42.230
has been a thing since the first book came out. People wondered after Ned Stark had his dream. Was he dreaming about Lyanna

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.370
having a baby?

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.370
Maybe that baby is Jon Snow?

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:52.219
Martin was probably always going to reveal that information in Winds of Winter. The problem is, is that even if he did, and that book

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.160
had been published years ago, before we got to season 6,

00:05:55.160 --> 00:06:00.890
the show still has to do a version of that. So if you're wondering why the show doesn't do more scenes like this,

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:04.549
it's just because they're not absolutely relevant for big information reveals.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:11.390
The only reason the show did this now is because they wanted to create drama between Jon Snow and Daenerys. Like create some cracks in

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.520
the Alliance. Create a reason for them not to be together.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:18.169
So if you're wondering why we haven't seen the Trident or other big Robert's Rebellion flashbacks,

00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:22.849
it's just because those scenes aren't necessary for what's happening in present day. So anytime

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:26.510
there's some contextual moment that they need and it's a really big book moment

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.230
That's what they tend to go for. But as for future flashbacks,

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:35.149
Just because the previous trend the last couple of seasons has been Jon Snow specific flashbacks,

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:39.919
I think that will continue to be the case so if we get season eight Trident flashbacks or something else

00:06:40.039 --> 00:06:44.389
I think they'll also continue to be about John Snow. But I feel like for the most part

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:49.728
they've answered all the questions they need to about his origins. He's the true born son of Rhaegar and Lyanna.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:55.380
He has a stronger claim to the throne than Daenerys now. Like Kit Harington makes that joke.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.289
"I can lord that over Emilia every day. " *laughs*

00:06:58.319 --> 00:06:59.520
"Every day."

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:04.849
Moving into undead ice dragon territory. This actually confirms some of the things that I previously

00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:12.258
thought. Like my initial take after the episode aired. People were wondering, "Why blue fire? Why does Viserion work this way, given

00:07:12.259 --> 00:07:18.379
what happened to him before?" The whole explainer is that it is the Night King's magic. He's breathing magical fire.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:22.309
He's flying by magic, whether you think it works, it doesn't work.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:26.239
That's what they were going for. I think the idea now is is, is he's more

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:33.020
powerful than the other dragons. Because Drogon is still the largest, I know it's kind of hard to tell because they're all so large now,

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:39.859
but Drogon is still proportionately larger than Viserion and Rhaegal. But I think I added it to a previous video, Neil deGrasse Tyson

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:46.669
was going all science on the episode where he said that the blue fire was basically three times hotter than regular fire.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:51.259
So even if you're not thinking about anything else with the Night King's magic, that by

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:58.070
itself would make Viserion more powerful than the other dragons. So the Night King has had a thousand years to perfect his magic. He gets

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:05.419
his hands on a dragon. He probably knows more about the dragons than Daenerys does and the other big thing, they don't quite clarify it here,

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.590
but the idea of whether or not

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:12.409
Viserion's blue fire can actually hurt Daenerys. The dragons are capable of killing each other,

00:08:12.409 --> 00:08:16.339
so I think that Daenerys is only resistant to Viserion's blue fire.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:20.329
But if she were to bathe in that, one, her clothes would all be incinerated

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:25.310
So she'd be naked after that. All of her hair would be singed off and she might get some third-degree burns,

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:30.589
but she could probably soak a little bit of damage and that's just going on the TV shows logic.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:34.880
Daenerys in the books is a little bit different. The way the blood magic protects her against the fire.

00:08:34.919 --> 00:08:40.158
But a lot of the way any of those battles go will depend on who's there to help them out because I don't think they're

00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:44.838
gonna do any of that by themselves. But the whole deal with that new short story that George R. R. Martin

00:08:44.839 --> 00:08:49.489
just published is that it's a sequel to the Princess and the Queen and the Rogue Prince. Dealing with

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:55.640
Targaryen kings after Aegon the conquerer. So the new one just deals with his two sons, It's actually pretty cool,

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:59.119
so I'll probably do a video on it in the next couple days and read a little bit from it.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:05.270
It's only about 26 pages long, but it's always fun to read those stories, and see how Martin invokes a lot of the stuff

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.419
that's happening in present day. Like there are a lot of themes that recur.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.969
There are a lot of people that have the same names like Samwell's

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:16.220
ancestor Samwell the Savage. So I know I also said I'd do a casting video for season 8.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:21.649
There are a couple minor roles that they're casting, so that'll come in the next couple days too- but tonight at midnight

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:26.899
they're dropping a trailer for the New Mutants movie. Maisie Williams is actually in that. She's playing

00:09:27.029 --> 00:09:34.099
Wolfsbane. So the "wolf" from Game of Thrones is playing a "wolf" in a Marvel movie. So that won't be till midnight tonight though.

